    {
      "id": "p0199-b009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Under normal circumstances, a professional translator would've immediately looked for the equivalent lines from the Japanese version of Kitchen. However, Toby specifically noted that he considered this text an \"in-joke between friends\" and that \"since it's just a joke, you don't have to find the original\". He further emphasized this attitude elsewhere in the spreadsheet by saying \"Another Banana Yoshimoto reference. Again, I don't care that much\".",
        "raw": "Under normal circumstances, a professional translator would've immediately\nlooked for the equivalent lines from the Japanese version of Kitchen. However,\nToby specifically noted that he considered this text an \"in-joke between friends\"\nand that \"since it's just a joke, you don't have to find the original\". He further\nemphasized this attitude elsewhere in the spreadsheet by saying \"Another\nBanana Yoshimoto reference. Again, I don't care that much\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.0966485,
          0.59693571,
          0.71126306,
          0.70058571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09366,
          0.59622143,
          0.71329605,
          0.70165714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          39,
          40,
          41,
          42,
          43,
          44
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "通常，专业译者会立刻去日文版《厨房》里寻找对应原句。但 Toby 特别说明，他把这段当成“朋友之间的内部笑话”，“既然只是个玩笑，就不用找原文了”。他在表格另一处又强调：“又是个吉本芭娜娜的引用。我还是没那么在意。”",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
