    {
      "id": "p0199-b011",
      "kind": "aside",
      "source": {
        "text": "Normally, skilled translators will go out of their way to retain jokes and references, as it's assumed that the original author considered them important enough to use. As such, it's rare to encounter a situation like this, in which the author is actually so unattached to a reference that the translators are asked to skip it! Toby truly is the king of crazy exceptions.",
        "raw": "Normally, skilled translators will go out of their way to retain jokes and\nreferences, as it's assumed that the original author considered them\nimportant enough to use. As such, it's rare to encounter a situation like\nthis, in which the author is actually so unattached to a reference that the\ntranslators are asked to skip it! Toby truly is the king of crazy exceptions.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.11543336,
          0.81074286,
          0.66798063,
          0.88510714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.11411192,
          0.81002857,
          0.66930207,
          0.88617857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          49,
          50,
          51,
          52,
          53
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "熟练的译者通常会特意保留笑话和引用，因为原作者既然用了，就应该认为它们值得保留。因此，这种情况很罕见：作者对某处引用竟如此不在意，反而要求译者跳过它！Toby 真是各种离奇例外之王。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
